<title>GERMANY: Fifth German beet test has 11.10 T/ha sugar yield.</title>
<headline>Fifth German beet test has 11.10 T/ha sugar yield.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The fifth German sugar beet test of the 1996/97 campaign showed a sugar yield of 11.10 tonnes per hectare compared with 10.08 tonnes in the fifth test of 1995/96, the sugar industry association WVZ said.  </p>
<p>The test also showed an average sugar content of 17.8 percent compared with 16.4 percent in the fifth 1995 test and 16.8 percent in the fourth test taken a fortnight ago, when the sugar yield was 9.71 tonnes/ha.</p>
<p>The fifth 1996 test was taken last Friday, September 27, and last year's fifth test was taken on September 30, 1995.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
